															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser deleted" data-id="1361261"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/common--images/avatars/default/a16.png" alt=""/>(account deleted)</span> <span class="odate time_1398968596 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">01 May 2014 18:23</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2023665">
									

<p>This is loaded with asstons of references and wacky people who do things for reasons. What it doesn't have is any narrative cohesion, characterization independent of what's already pre-packaged from site non-canon canon, or a reason that I should be interested in this.</p>
<p>I'll keep an open mind through this exercise, but by definition this can't have any idea of where it's going, which is sort of necessary for telling an actual story. Tossing a mixture of random bits and lolsozany pellets into the plot blunderbuss and firing it at an article isn't really doing much for me.</p>

							</div>

								
					
